chieve we  are in a way immediately then  establishing a new baseline or barometer  for our lives and still then looking to  the next thing and I fall into this as  well with this program right which is  every time we set a goal for the show  and and you know knock on wood so far we  achieve those goals immediately I start  thinking of the next thing and it's this  constant treadmill that doesn't really  allow you to just say okay now is when  I'm in a good place  yeah absolutely and it's you know again  a big part of that is the  misunderstanding that okay when I hit  this mark whatever that is then I'm  gonna feel a certain way right we tied  the mark to how we feel when they're not  really related it's not like I mean yeah  pirata marathon or you hit some big  business milestone sure you're gonna be  happy for a little while but that is not  where sustainable long term peace of  mind and happiness come from at all and  so we're just on this treadmill of like  oh the next thing and then we hit the  goal we don't feel the way we thought  we'd feel so we think well maybe that  was the wrong goal maybe I didn't really  want this I wanted this other thing so  then we're all running after the next  day has this existed as long as humans  have I mean I I because we I only exist  now right so it's very hard for me to  say well this is a dynamic this is this  is a phenomena that would have been  observed twenty thirty thousand years  ago for humans on the one hand humans  have not changed all that much in recent  time but at the same time we have a  completely unique life situation right  now the day-to-day concerns for life are  so different now than they were ten  thousand years ago I wonder about that  I do too that's an excellent question I  I don't know I would love to go back to  cute man days and see what their minds  did you know and what they thought about  ahead and goals and all of that I mean I  think clearly our society today doesn't  help so you know but the